n19236.content:
\begin{theorem}[Bernoulli depth-tail probability monotonicity]
\lean{LMN.bernoulliRestrProb_dtDepth_compose_le}
\label{LMN.bernoulliRestrProb_dtDepth_compose_le}
\leanok
\uses{LMN.composeRestr, LMN.dtDepth_composeRestr_le, LMN.restriction_compose_eq, SwitchingLemma2.bernoulliRestrProb, SwitchingLemma2.bernoulliRestrProb_le_one', SwitchingLemma2.bernoulliRestrWeight, SwitchingLemma2.bernoulliRestrWeight_nonneg', SwitchingLemma2.restrictFn, dtDepth}

For every Boolean function $f$, threshold $t$, and parameters $p_1, p_2 \in (0,1]$, the
probability that the restricted depth exceeds $t$ under the stronger Bernoulli restriction
of parameter $p_1 p_2$ is at most that under parameter $p_1$:
\[
  \Pr_{p_1 p_2}\bigl[\mathrm{dtDepth}(f|_\rho) > t\bigr] \le
  \Pr_{p_1}\bigl[\mathrm{dtDepth}(f|_\rho) > t\bigr].
\]
\end{theorem}

