n19370.content:
\begin{theorem}[Clause indices are nodup (AND)]
\lean{BoolCircuit.NAndCircuit.clause_nodup}
\label{BoolCircuit.NAndCircuit.clause_nodup}
\leanok
\uses{BoolCircuit.Lit, BoolCircuit.NAndCircuit}

If a normal-form AND circuit $c$ equals a clause built from literals $lits$ with a
duplication-free proof $h$, then the variable indices $lits.\mathrm{map}\;\mathrm{Lit.idx}$
are pairwise distinct.
