\leanok

A technical lemma: if $g(h\,c) = f\,c$ for all $c \in cs$, then the conjunctive
\texttt{foldr} of $g$ over $cs.\mathrm{map}\;h$ equals the conjunctive \texttt{foldr} of
$f$ over $cs$.
\end{theorem}

