\texttt{foldr} of $g$ over $cs.\mathrm{map}\;h$ equals the disjunctive \texttt{foldr} of
$f$ over $cs$.
\end{theorem}

n19377.content:
\begin{theorem}[Fold commutes with map (addition)]
\lean{BoolCircuit.foldr_add_map}
\label{BoolCircuit.foldr_add_map}
\leanok

A technical lemma: if $g(h\,c) = f\,c$ for all $c \in cs$, then the additive
\texttt{foldr} of $g$ over $cs.\mathrm{map}\;h$ equals the additive \texttt{foldr} of $f$
over $cs$.
\end{theorem}

n19378.content:
\begin{theorem}[Fold inequality under map (addition)]
\lean{BoolCircuit.foldr_add_map_le}
\label{BoolCircuit.foldr_add_map_le}
\leanok

A technical lemma: if $g(h\,c) \le k \cdot f\,c$ for all $c \in cs$, then the additive
