\leanok
\uses{Literal, Literal.eval, SwitchingLemma2.Literal.killedBy, SwitchingLemma2.Restriction, SwitchingLemma2.Restriction.extend}

If a literal $l$ is killed by $\rho$, then for every $x$ it evaluates to false on the
extended point: $l.\mathrm{eval}(\rho.\mathrm{extend}\,x) = \mathrm{false}$.
\end{lemma}

n19470.content:
