\lean{SwitchingLemma2.Literal.fixedBy_eval_true}
\label{SwitchingLemma2.Literal.fixedBy_eval_true}
\leanok
\uses{Literal, Literal.eval, SwitchingLemma2.Literal.fixedBy, SwitchingLemma2.Restriction, SwitchingLemma2.Restriction.extend}

If a literal $l$ is fixed by $\rho$, then for every $x$ it evaluates to true on the
extended point: $l.\mathrm{eval}(\rho.\mathrm{extend}\,x) = \mathrm{true}$.
\end{lemma}

n19471.content:
\begin{lemma}[Decision-tree depth bound from a witnessing tree]
