For all $x' : X'$ and $y' : Y'$,
$(p.\mathrm{comap}\,f_X\,f_Y).\mathrm{run}\,x'\,y' = p.\mathrm{run}\,(f_X\,x')\,(f_Y\,y')$.
\end{theorem}

n19574.content:
\begin{theorem}[Pullback preserves complexity]
\lean{CommunicationComplexity.Deterministic.FiniteMessage.Protocol.comap_complexity}
