Let $f, g : \{0,1\}^n \to \{0,1\}$, let $S \subseteq [n]$, and suppose
$\texttt{BoolBLR.lift\_pm1}\,g = \chi_S$ and $\dist(f, g) \ge \varepsilon$.
Then the Fourier coefficient of $\texttt{BoolBLR.lift\_pm1}\,f$ at $S$
satisfies $\widehat{\texttt{BoolBLR.lift\_pm1}\,f}(S) \le 1 - 2\varepsilon$.
\end{lemma}

n19897.content:
\begin{lemma}[Fourier coefficient bound when $\varepsilon$-far from linear]
\lean{BoolBLR.fourier_coeff_le_of_far_from_linear}
