Let $\mu$ be a distribution on $X \times Y$, let $g : X \to Y \to \mathrm{Bool}$, and
let $\varepsilon, \gamma \in \mathbb{R}$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$.  If every combinatorial
rectangle $R$ satisfies $|\mathrm{disc}_\mu(g,R)| \le \gamma$, and if
$2^n \cdot \gamma < 1 - 2\varepsilon$, then $n < \mathrm{CC}(g,\varepsilon)$ (the
public-coin $\varepsilon$-error communication complexity of $g$).
\end{theorem}

