Assume $X$ is nonempty and $L$ is a continuous linear functional on $u \to \mathbb{R}$
with $L(z) < L(c)$ for every $z \in U(X,f,u)$, where $c$ is a fixed vector. Then
$L(e_y) \le 0$ for every coordinate $y \in u$.
\end{lemma}

